Vikram and Betal: The Wise Old Woman

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was an old woman who lived in a small village,” said Betal. “She was poor but very wise.”

One day, two men came to her with a problem.

They were arguing over a pot of coins.

Each one said, “This pot belongs to me!”

The old woman listened carefully.

She said, “Leave the pot with me and come back tomorrow.”

That night, she looked closely at the pot and noticed a small mark on it.

The next day, both men returned.

She asked them, “Can you describe the pot?”

One man described the mark correctly.

The other could not.

The old woman gave the pot to the honest man.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the old woman wise?”

Vikram replied, “She listened carefully and observed closely before deciding.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Careful thinking leads to the right decision.
